  ('00818516-e7c6-515a-93f1-aab9410e1038', 'scheme-check-synthetic-v1', 'scheme_check', 'synthetic', 'cambridge', 'Further Mathematics 9231', '{"syllabus_code": "9231", "paper": "9231/11 Synthetic eval paper", "label": "2", "marks_available": 5, "question_text": "Prove by induction that 1 + 3 + 5 + ... + (2n - 1) = n^2 for every positive integer n.", "student_answer": "n = 1: 1 = 1^2 true. Assume true for n = k: sum = k^2. Then sum to k+1 = k^2 + 2k + 1 = (k+1)^2. So true for k+1. Since true for n=1 and true for k implies true for k+1, true for all positive integers.", "scheme": "Base case shown | B1\nState the inductive hypothesis for n = k | B1\nAdd the (k+1)th term to the hypothesis | M1\nReach (k+1)^2 | A1\nCorrect conclusion | A1", "conventions": "M: method mark, earned for a valid method even with an arithmetic slip. A: accuracy mark, needs the M mark it depends on. B: independent mark. FT: follow through from an earlier error.", "expected": {"can_check": true, "est": [5, 5], "control": null}}'::jsonb, '{"expected": {"can_check": true, "est": [5, 5], "control": null}, "draft": true}'::jsonb, true, array[]::text[]),
